---
import BlogPost from '../../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
import { withUtm, track } from '../../lib/links';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const listingSlug = 'assets-export-manager-for-jira-service-management';
const listing = withUtm('https://marketplace.atlassian.com/apps/3829199441/assets-export-manager-for-jira-service-management', listingSlug, 'blog-post');
const listingTrack = track('atlassian', listingSlug, 'blog-post');
const rows = [
  ['Insight Assets Backup & Migration', 'Twinit', '4.9 (30 reviews)', 'USD 1,520', 'Backup, restore, and migration of schemas, objects, and attachments', 'https://marketplace.atlassian.com/search?query=Insight%20Assets%20Backup%20%26%20Migration'],
  ['Assets Attachments Backup & Migration', 'Twinit', '5.0 (1 review)', 'see listing', 'Attachment-focused companion to the above', 'https://marketplace.atlassian.com/search?query=Assets%20Attachments%20Backup'],
  ['Assets Export Manager for JSM', 'Katabarwa Labs', 'new listing', 'USD 850', 'Whole-schema export to CSV or JSON, generated in-tenant and streamed to the browser; Runs on Atlassian', 'https://marketplace.atlassian.com/apps/3829199441/assets-export-manager-for-jira-service-management'],
];
---
<BlogPost
  title="JSM Assets export and backup apps compared: whole-schema export versus backup and restore"
  description="Twinit's Insight Assets Backup & Migration and Assets Export Manager compared on what they cover, whether they can restore, where the data goes, and list price at 100 users, next to the native per-object-type export."
  tag="Jira Service Management"
  pubDate="September 10, 2026"
  readMins={6}
  image="/apps/jsm-assets-export/h1.png"
  app="jsm-assets-export"
>
  <p>
    Disclosure first: Assets Export Manager is ours. Facts are from the public Marketplace listings as
    of September 2026, prices at the 100-user tier. The native starting point is Atlassian's own
    <a class="text-brand" href="https://support.atlassian.com/jira-service-management-cloud/docs/export-objects/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">export objects</a>
    feature, which exports one object type at a time to CSV; the request for a whole-schema export,
    <a class="text-brand" href="https://jira.atlassian.com/browse/JSDCLOUD-9967" target="_blank" rel="noopener">JSDCLOUD-9967</a>, has hundreds of votes.
  </p>

  <h2>Export versus backup</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Backup and restore.</strong> Twinit's products copy schemas, objects, and attachments so
      you can restore or migrate them, including into another site. That is the job if you need to
      recover from a bad bulk edit or move a CMDB between instances.</li>
    <li><strong>A portable copy of the whole schema.</strong> Every object type and attribute in one
      CSV or JSON, for an auditor, a migration baseline, or offline analysis. Assets Export Manager
      does exactly that and nothing else: it pages the schema in your tenant and streams the file to
      your browser. It cannot restore, and it does not export attachment binaries.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The apps, side by side</h2>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full text-[14.5px]">
      <thead><tr class="border-b border-line text-left text-muted"><th class="py-2 pr-3">App</th><th class="py-2 pr-3">Vendor</th><th class="py-2 pr-3">Rating</th><th class="py-2 pr-3">List price, 100 users, per year</th><th class="py-2">What it does</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {rows.map((r) => (
          <tr class="border-b border-line align-top">
            <td class="py-2 pr-3 font-semibold"><a class="text-brand" href={r[5]} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{r[0]}</a></td>
            <td class="py-2 pr-3">{r[1]}</td><td class="py-2 pr-3">{r[2]}</td><td class="py-2 pr-3">{r[3]}</td><td class="py-2">{r[4]}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>How to choose</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>You might need to put objects back.</strong> Backup and restore, full stop.</li>
    <li><strong>You need the register out, whole, on demand.</strong> A whole-schema export. Ours is
      bounded per run and marks a truncated export honestly rather than silently cutting it.</li>
    <li><strong>Assets pricing is per Jira user, not per agent.</strong> Every app in this category is
      billed on the Jira user tier of the whole instance, which is Atlassian's model rather than any
      vendor's. Run your real user count through the calculators.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Our tool:</strong> <a class="text-brand font-semibold" href={listing} {...listingTrack} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Assets Export Manager for JSM</a>
    on the Atlassian Marketplace, and the <a class="text-brand font-semibold" href={`${base}/atlassian/jsm-assets-export`}>product page</a>.
  </div>

  <p class="mt-6">
    Related reading:
    <a class="text-brand" href={`${base}/blog/export-jsm-assets-object-schema`}>How to bulk-export a JSM Assets object schema (CSV or JSON)</a>.
  </p>
</BlogPost>
